= Charlottesville

Torch-bearing white supremacists march through a Virginia college town. One of them drives a car into a crowd of counter-protesters, killing a woman. The president's response draws bipartisan criticism. Organized extremism has stepped out of the shadows.

- @condemn: Unite the country in condemnation.
- @confront: Confront the far right in the streets.
- @legal: Press for stronger domestic-extremism enforcement.

@condemn
subtitle: Moral clarity, broad appeal.
on-arrival: stability += 3; media_trust += 2; enthusiasm += 2; far_right -= 2

Leaders of both parties speak against hatred. The rally leaders are shunned.

@confront
subtitle: Risky, can escalate.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 4; far_left += 3; far_right += 2; stability -= 2; pop_mod -= 0.1

Counter-protests grow. Some are peaceful. Some are not. The fringes feed on each other.

@legal
subtitle: Institutional.
on-arrival: far_right -= 4; stability += 2; prog_dissent += 2

Civil libertarians worry about the tools. Law enforcement welcomes the attention.
